


RWALL(3R)           UNIX Programmer's Manual            RWALL(3R)



NAME
     rwall - write to specified remote machines

SYNOPSIS
     #include <rpcsvc/rwall.h>
9     rwall(host, msg);
          char *host, *msg;

DESCRIPTION
     _R_w_a_l_l causes _h_o_s_t to print the string _m_s_g to all its users.
     It returns 0 if successful.

RPC INFO
     program number:
          WALLPROG
9     procs:
          WALLPROC_WALL
               Takes string as argument (wrapstring), returns no arguments.
               Executes _w_a_l_l on remote host with string.
     versions:
          RSTATVERS_ORIG

SEE ALSO
     rwall(1), shutdown(8), rwalld(8C)






























